## Soteria execution monitoring (FR-009).
##
## Installed as /etc/audit/rules.d/soteria.rules and loaded by auditd
## (augenrules). It asks the kernel to report every successful program
## execution; Soteria reads these events from the audit multicast stream
## with CAP_AUDIT_READ and never changes audit rules itself.
##
## auditd also writes these events to its own log (/var/log/audit), which
## grows with the number of executions; size it with max_log_file and
## num_logs in /etc/audit/auditd.conf.
-a always,exit -F arch=b64 -S execve,execveat -F success=1 -F key=soteria_exec
## 32-bit programs use a separate system call table; without this rule they
## would run unseen on 64-bit hosts that support them.
-a always,exit -F arch=b32 -S execve,execveat -F success=1 -F key=soteria_exec
